-- FLEET-TWIN-BASELINE-1 (2026-11-05, charter pillar autonomy; roadmap_implementation 3259 RM-BS-FLEET-TWIN-1, PR 7664; blue-sky bet B3 step one, program QNFO.OPS; session W2-H).
-- WHAT: row 3259 goes planned -> partial. Slice one is code: qnfo-deploy-guard 1.5.0 GET /twin/baseline (reverts per deploy, restore time as an upper bound, drills apart) and
--   scripts/deploy_probes.py --preview (a worker probes.json run against an uploaded version through Cloudflare-Workers-Version-Overrides, with a routing proof). No new metric is registered:
--   the baseline is a read surface, and the BP26 change_failure_rate keeps its own producer (the follow-up row .3 below widens what it counts).
-- WHY partial, not built: the doc names previews that gate a merge, a percentage canary with seconds-level rollback, a replay twin, TLA+ specs, a tamper audit and code-loop attempts in Artifacts. This
--   slice measures the baseline those are judged against and makes the preview probe honest. Remaining, in order: (.2) gradual_deploy.py deploys the candidate at 0 percent before the override smoke and runs
--   probes.json on it (filed below); (.3) BP26 change_failure_rate counts probe reverts (filed below); then adoption of the first worker in scripts/gradual-deploy-workers.txt, the replay twin, TLA+ and the tamper audit (W2).
-- LIVE FINDINGS (read 2026-11-05): a version override naming an unknown version id, and one naming the previous uploaded version that is not in the current deployment, were both ignored and answered by production
--   (qnfo-deploy-guard /health: 200, VERSION 1.4.7). Cloudflare docs (Version overrides): an override is applied only if the version is in the current deployment. Worker Previews (changelog 2026-09-22): KV, D1 and R2
--   are isolated only when a Preview binds a separate resource; Version URLs and overrides use production bindings. The blue-sky doc says preview isolation of D1 and KV is undocumented: it is documented, and it is not isolated by default.
-- PREDICTION (decision_log): GET /twin/baseline answers 200 with deploys.in_window above 1000 and a change_failure_rate within 25 minutes of the deploy; reverts per 100 deploys over 30 days reads between 0.1 and 1.0.
--   Falsifier: the route answers 5xx, deploys.in_window reads 0, or the canary reverts qnfo-deploy-guard 1.5.0.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- BACKUP: bak_20261105_fleet_twin_roadmap
-- Rollback: UPDATE roadmap_implementation SET status = (SELECT b.status FROM bak_20261105_fleet_twin_roadmap b WHERE b.id = roadmap_implementation.id), evidence = (SELECT b.evidence FROM bak_20261105_fleet_twin_roadmap b WHERE b.id = roadmap_implementation.id) WHERE id = 3259; UPDATE agent_issues SET status = 'closed' WHERE source = 'session:W2-H-3259' AND title LIKE 'ROADMAP-1: QNFO.OPS RM-BS-FLEET-TWIN-1.%'
-- CAUSE-MAPPED: registers no metric_registry row; the follow-up rows carry code-probe contracts.

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261105_fleet_twin_roadmap AS SELECT * FROM roadmap_implementation WHERE id = 3259;

UPDATE roadmap_implementation SET status = 'partial', evidence = COALESCE(evidence, '') || ' | ' || 'W2-H 2026-11-05 (PR 7664): slice one shipped. qnfo-deploy-guard 1.5.0 serves GET https://qnfo-deploy-guard.q08.workers.dev/twin/baseline?days=7..40 (open, read-only, KV-cached 10 min): denominator bp26_deploy_events without the retired root stub, numerator the canary revert issues (CONTROL-PLANE-REVERTED-1, DEPLOY-PROBE-REVERTED-1, *-CANARY-FAILED-1; DEPLOY-PROBE-FAILED-1 apart), per-worker rows, restore time as an upper bound (previous recorded deployment to the next one; p95 null below five restores), the DEPLOY-PROBES drills (49ce59b, a339688) counted apart, a revert before the first recorded deployment listed and not counted; suite qnfo-deploy-guard/twin-baseline.test.mjs (27 checks) and a probe in qnfo-deploy-guard/probes.json. scripts/deploy_probes.py --preview <worker> --version-id <id> [--expect-version <VERSION>] runs the declared HTTP probes of a worker against an uploaded version (preview_check, 80 selftest checks): a failure is re-run on production so a failure on both is pre-existing, D1 EXPLAIN probes and other hosts are skipped with the reason, and routing must be observed (the candidate VERSION on /health with the override) or the run is inconclusive. Correction to the doc: the BP26 change_failure_rate counted CONTROL-PLANE-REVERTED-1 only (probe reverts were not failures there) and mttr_rollback_min_p95 is UNMEASURED below five rollbacks. Live finding: an override to an unknown or not-in-deployment version is answered by production (read on qnfo-deploy-guard), so a preview probe is only evidence when routing is observed. Primary docs read: Worker Previews isolate KV/D1/R2 only through a separate bound resource; Version URLs and overrides use production bindings. Open: ROADMAP-1 QNFO.OPS RM-BS-FLEET-TWIN-1.2 (0 percent deployment before the override smoke in scripts/gradual_deploy.py, then probes.json on it), .3 (BP26 counts probe reverts), then first worker on the gradual allowlist, replay twin, TLA+ specs, tamper audit (W2 of the doc).' WHERE id = 3259 AND item = 'RM-BS-FLEET-TWIN-1' AND instr(COALESCE(evidence, ''), 'W2-H 2026-11-05') = 0;

INSERT INTO agent_issues (title, description, source, category, priority, status, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT 'ROADMAP-1: QNFO.OPS RM-BS-FLEET-TWIN-1.2: gradual_deploy.py deploys the candidate at 0 percent before the override smoke and runs probes.json on it',
 'QNFO.OPS; charter pillar autonomy; roadmap row 3259 (RM-BS-FLEET-TWIN-1); doer: qnfo-code-orchestrator via the code-task line. Metric it should move: deploys_via_gradual (above 0 once a worker is on scripts/gradual-deploy-workers.txt and a push stages) and change_failure_rate (reverts per 100 deploys in GET https://qnfo-deploy-guard.q08.workers.dev/twin/baseline). Verified 2026-11-05: scripts/gradual_deploy.py run() uploads a Version and smoke-tests it with Cloudflare-Workers-Version-Overrides before any deployment contains it; Cloudflare applies an override only when the version is in the current deployment, and on qnfo-deploy-guard an override to an uploaded version that was not in the current deployment was answered by production (VERSION 1.4.7 for the previous version id 6f834d3a-07ec-4715-98ea-9a69086ad727). The smoke loop then waits for a VERSION that cannot arrive, which fits the staged path never having rolled out a worker (the allowlist holds none). Work: (1) in run(), after the upload, create a deployment with the new version at 0 percent and the previous version at 100 (deploy(api, acct, worker, [(new, 0), (prev, 100)], ...)), then run the smoke test with the override; a smoke failure deploys the previous version at 100 again; (2) after /health reports the new VERSION, call deploy_probes.preview_check(decl, worker, new, expect_version=want) for the worker probes.json (scripts/deploy_probes.py, merged in PR 7664) and treat a regression as a failed smoke test, an inconclusive or none state as pass-with-note, recording preview_probes in RESULT_JSON; (3) selftest cases for the 0 percent step and a preview regression. Carry the tag RM-BS-FLEET-TWIN-1.2 in a comment at the edit. scripts/gradual_deploy.py was under work claim by B-governance-code (GRADUAL-ES-MODULE-1) until 2026-11-05T04:30Z: review that change first and build on it. Done: merged, python3 scripts/gradual_deploy.py --selftest passes, and one staged run (gradual-deploy.yml workflow_dispatch on a non-control-plane worker) shows RESULT_JSON with smoke routing observed. Failure mode: a 0 percent deployment makes Cloudflare serve two versions at once, so a worker with a Durable Object migration or a cron change cannot use the path (documented exception in docs/GRADUAL-DEPLOYS.md).' || char(10) || char(10) ||
 'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=scripts/gradual_deploy.py' || char(10) ||
 'code-anchor: def run(worker, acct, token, path=None, stages=(10, 50, 100), soak=120, dry=False, api=None, sleep=time.sleep, fetch=fetch_health, now=time.time, emit=print):' || char(10) ||
 'code-probe: {"paths":["scripts/gradual_deploy.py"],"contains":"RM-BS-FLEET-TWIN-1.2"}',
 'session:W2-H-3259', 'code', 'medium', 'open', unixepoch() * 1000, unixepoch() * 1000
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'ROADMAP-1: QNFO.OPS RM-BS-FLEET-TWIN-1.2:%' AND status = 'open');

